  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "subterraneo",
      "id": "LUG-04",
      "plano": "subterraneo",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.jg1zpvYlDFMJRY8Q]{The Sealed Underground (Seattle Underground)}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.5hwXPdn0tUJ3NaKZ.JournalEntryPage.lM1EiE1FoXMkf3Uo]{A1-E04 · Everything Sells Below}</p>\n<p><strong>Arrival (A1-E04, Nights 2 to 4).</strong> A staircase leads down from a Pioneer Square basement (west) to the <strong>iron door</strong> that appears on no map. Behind it, the 1889 brick sidewalk runs east beneath the city: boarded-up shopfronts on both sides of the Market&#39;s entrance, <strong>violet glass skylights</strong> in the ceiling (Foundry lights over the sidewalk, nothing painted), and a <strong>network cable</strong> running along the top of the south wall to Ezra&#39;s door. It smells of mold, of damp, and, every so often, of server ozone.</p>\n<p><strong>The Undermarket.</strong> The big shop in the middle, open to the sidewalk through its cast-iron columns. Stalls of information and favors (fixed, painted) and two stall lanterns. <strong>Rules Below:</strong> no fighting in the Market, everything has a price, and nobody asks about anybody&#39;s face. Fighting here turns Thornquist and a dozen runners against the coterie and shuts off LOR-02.</p>\n<p><strong>The barbershop (Thornquist&#39;s office).</strong> At the far east end of the sidewalk, “there&#39;s a carbide lamp burning”: you can see it from a distance through the shopfront window, the only one that still has its glass. Thornquist receives visitors seated in the <strong>barber&#39;s chair</strong> (fixed, bolted to the floor) “as if it were a throne.” The carbide lamp is a lit tile (<code>tile-lampara-carburo</code>) on the counter. In the back corner, the <strong>safe</strong> with the duplicates of USB drives 1 and 2 (AVE-01-AJUSTE; Krell doesn&#39;t know they exist). Tests: Manipulation + Persuasion Diff. 4 (Ezra +2), Wits + Insight Diff. 3.</p>\n<p><strong>Ezra&#39;s nest (PJ-03, Haven 2).</strong> Under the street, across from the barbershop: racks of salvaged servers, the desk with his monitors (“screen” light), and the cot. The network cable from the sidewalk comes in through his door; the cables “come down through nineteenth-century holes” in the ceiling.</p>\n<p><strong>The thin-blood shelter.</strong> An old coal vault under the street: mattresses, blankets, candles, and the heap of coal nobody ever cleared out. Jun Takeda (PNJ-20) hasn&#39;t been back since the Pier 46 business: if they look for her here, she isn&#39;t here (she sleeps in a storage unit in SoDo).</p>\n<p><strong>LOR-02.</strong> The boarded-up shopfronts open onto abandoned shops with no door (the boards are nailed over the wall); if a PC has “Sealed Haven” (•••), the Storyteller can open one with a secret door.</p>\n<p><strong>Off the map.</strong> The staircase climbs to Pioneer Square (no street map). The sidewalk continues east behind a brick partition wall.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (3) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<div class=\"sbn-figuras\"><p><strong>Placed tokens.</strong> Hidden ones are revealed from the token layer; the ones that depend on how the night went say when.</p><ul><li>@UUID[Actor.NDI68PA4J59Be6ts]{Abel Thornquist} (A1-E04): In the barber&#39;s chair, “as if it were a throne.”</li></ul></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> Up to Pioneer Square.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
